   :summary
   "Executive summary:\n\n- The contracts are overwhelmingly similar in structure and content. The principal substantive differences are:\n  1. Version 3.1.1 removes the explicit Minimum Required Domestic Content Level (60%) and the representation that solar PV Facilities meet that level. This is the single most material change and alters a supplier compliance/warranty obligation present in Version 2.0.\n  2. Version 3.1.1 revises the data collection/disclosure language: it removes explicit references to collecting GST number and domestic content compliance information, and adds an express allowance to disclose facility details to other government ministries/agencies for public health, safety and emergency planning/response. This broadens certain permitted disclosures while narrowing explicitly-listed data examples.\n  3. Version 3.1.1 adds a procedural requirement that certain notifications be made 'in the Prescribed Form', creating an administrative/formality requirement not present in Version 2.0.\n\n- Recommended immediate actions:\n  - Confirm whether program-level rules (outside the contract text) still require domestic content — if so, ensure contract/version selection aligns with enforcement and eligibility practices.\n  - Obtain the 'Prescribed Form' and update supplier notification and compliance processes accordingly.\n  - Review privacy/data-sharing procedures and update supplier communications to reflect the explicit emergency/public-safety disclosure in Version 3.1.1."},
